  "summary": "Coarse-grained, constant-pH and all-atom simulations now resolve chromatin pairing, condensate pKa shifts and complex I proton-gating switches.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that local environment sets the protonation and conformational states that govern molecular behaviour, probed by simulation across scales. Coarse-grained work extends Helical Coherence Theory to multi-persistence-length dsDNA under spherical confinement, reporting non-monotonic, ion-dependent pairing dynamics relevant to homologous gene pairing. All-atom constant-pH molecular dynamics of phase-separated condensates finds protonated states favoured, shifting residue pKa values relative to bulk solvent. Simulations of respiratory complex I show histidine switch dynamics coupled to lysine charge states, which may gate proton transfer. What is new across these studies is the explicit treatment of confinement, condensate solvation and charge-state coupling as direct modulators of molecular behaviour rather than fixed backdrop. The thread is not uniform: the DNA study addresses ion-dependent geometry, while the other two address protonation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-01-17"
}
